WEBVTT

01:03.980 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:06.066 --> 01:07.776
Oh, that Ae-sun!

01:07.859 --> 01:10.361
-Whoa. Hey! Come on! Stop!
-That damn Ae-sun! Ae-sun, damn you!

01:10.445 --> 01:12.072
-Goodness, Mother.
-What did I do?

01:12.155 --> 01:14.783
-Please, Mother!
-I told your grandson no!

01:14.866 --> 01:17.077
-That child!
-I said, "No, thank you." All right?

01:17.160 --> 01:19.579
-That damn girl! Ae-sun!
-Oh my God!

01:19.662 --> 01:21.915
Nana, why are you doing this? Why, why?

01:21.998 --> 01:23.541
What?

01:24.667 --> 01:27.504
Tell me why you'd ruin
someone else's cabbages like that.

01:27.587 --> 01:29.380
Why, you little…

01:29.464 --> 01:32.258
She said, "No, thanks. No, thank you."

01:53.655 --> 01:55.240
Barnacles and conches.

01:57.367 --> 01:59.869
A haenyeo's daughter
and a fish seller's son.

02:00.453 --> 02:01.788
Same difference.

02:02.872 --> 02:04.874
It's not like you are nobility.

02:26.563 --> 02:29.274
Nothing will happen
just 'cause we hang out.

02:30.483 --> 02:32.944
Yeah, I mean, I simply wanna sit
next to somebody's store

02:33.027 --> 02:34.696
so I can run my family business.

02:35.196 --> 02:37.699
It's not like I'm obsessed
with finding a husband.

02:39.951 --> 02:41.828
I wouldn't get hitched to you anyway,

02:42.579 --> 02:43.955
even if they made me.

02:44.038 --> 02:45.081
I'm not crazy.

02:45.165 --> 02:48.126
Why would I marry an island guy?
All my roots are in Seoul.

02:48.209 --> 02:49.252
A store in Gyeonggi.

02:50.086 --> 02:51.462
Your uncle operates one.

02:52.297 --> 02:53.131
In Gyeonggi.

02:53.214 --> 02:54.799
Yeah, and Gyeonggi is nearly Seoul.

03:00.805 --> 03:03.099
Damn sea swallowed up
my mother and my father.

03:03.183 --> 03:05.977
Makes me sick seeing those waves
come from every direction.

03:06.060 --> 03:07.312
You think I'd settle here?

03:07.812 --> 03:10.940
I'm going to marry a man from Seoul,
no matter what.

03:11.024 --> 03:12.525
I won't marry an islander.

03:13.318 --> 03:17.071
Especially anyone that can't comprehend
what "nostalgia" is.

03:17.155 --> 03:18.239
Never!

03:21.618 --> 03:24.621
Cat got your tongue or what?
Why aren't you saying anything?

03:25.705 --> 03:28.208
God, I'd rather hang with
a dolhareubang statue.

03:28.291 --> 03:30.043
So take your hand out of my pocket

03:30.710 --> 03:32.128
since I'm not a guy from Seoul.

03:52.607 --> 03:54.400
Give away your son if you like.

03:55.109 --> 03:58.738
It sure looks like you're totally fine
giving him away to that girl.

03:59.322 --> 04:00.990
I'd never go against your word, would I?

04:01.074 --> 04:02.075
You would.

04:03.534 --> 04:04.827
You arrived knocked up.

04:05.328 --> 04:06.704
Don't be too harsh on them.

04:06.788 --> 04:09.999
It could make them go too far.
You know what I mean, right?

04:10.083 --> 04:12.627
I know.
That's why I was so darn mad.

04:12.710 --> 04:14.087
If we leave them alone,

04:14.170 --> 04:16.339
they'll run away
in the middle of the night

04:16.422 --> 04:18.549
right under your nose, just like you did.

04:18.633 --> 04:23.513
So you're saying that
I robbed you of your son, is that right?

04:23.596 --> 04:26.474
Rumors spread like wildfire
on a small island like ours.

04:26.557 --> 04:28.518
Everyone knows what you did back then.

04:28.601 --> 04:31.187
Why are you pretending to be
such a saint, huh?

04:31.271 --> 04:34.148
Well, he's just a teen.
They'll be together a bit and move on.

04:34.232 --> 04:35.775
Leave them alone.

04:35.858 --> 04:39.153
Once they've had enough, they'll stop.
Why is it so concerning to you?

04:39.237 --> 04:40.863
Not much we can do, you know.

04:41.364 --> 04:44.867
Yes, the sons in our two families
really have been idiots.

04:45.410 --> 04:49.455
They have been confused for generations,
and I'm the mean wench who's crazy.

04:50.790 --> 04:52.125
Leave them alone.

04:53.251 --> 04:56.504
He wouldn't bring a beggar in
just because he feels guilty, right?

04:56.587 --> 04:57.422
Hmm?

05:09.309 --> 05:10.685
Giving us seer fish today?

05:12.228 --> 05:13.771
Well, aren't we the lucky ones?

05:14.355 --> 05:16.524
Can't believe we get so many freebies.

05:17.567 --> 05:20.528
If I fed people I felt bad for,
I'd give that to a beggar.

05:21.029 --> 05:22.030
At school,

05:22.530 --> 05:24.866
you always used to give me
your leftover milk,

05:24.949 --> 05:27.160
and… I'm so damn grateful.

05:28.453 --> 05:30.872
You think I gave you fish
for ten years out of pity?

05:31.414 --> 05:33.333
So why do you do it?

05:33.416 --> 05:35.793
You think I'd be a moron for ten years?

05:36.294 --> 05:37.962
So why are you giving them to us?

05:38.755 --> 05:40.506
It's about damn time you told me.

05:43.509 --> 05:44.469
What are you looking at?

05:45.303 --> 05:47.638
Look me in the eye for once
and say something.

05:49.515 --> 05:51.684
You give me food
and never do anything else.

05:52.477 --> 05:56.064
What, your grandma say to give us fish
but to keep your mouth shut?

05:56.606 --> 05:58.733
Did she tell you not to waste your breath?

06:06.616 --> 06:08.409
Damn little runt of a man.

06:09.452 --> 06:11.204
You're such a brat.

06:14.123 --> 06:15.541
Do you kiss little runt men?

06:15.625 --> 06:16.751
That was my philtrum.

06:16.834 --> 06:18.294
I wouldn't kiss beggars either.

06:18.378 --> 06:20.213
Uh… Hold on, um,

06:20.797 --> 06:23.257
so you like me, is that it, huh?

06:23.341 --> 06:26.010
I want to be living with you.
Not… not with my grandma.

06:27.929 --> 06:28.971
Oh, um,

06:29.764 --> 06:32.308
but why would you kiss my philtrum,

06:32.392 --> 06:33.976
and after I, well--

06:34.060 --> 06:35.353
Oh my God, just shut up already!

06:35.937 --> 06:38.606
What's with you? Your mouth is going,
and you keep saying things,

06:38.689 --> 06:40.817
and I have no idea
what you're talking about.

06:41.317 --> 06:44.153
You're the brat who puts her hand
in my pocket. What am I supposed to say?

06:44.237 --> 06:46.447
-What's with your glossy lips every day?
-I wear lipstick!

06:46.531 --> 06:47.490
-Why?
-So I'm ready.

06:47.573 --> 06:48.699
Uh, what?

06:49.492 --> 06:50.910
Oh shit.

06:51.661 --> 06:54.914
I've been ready since I was 14, and, uh…

07:18.896 --> 07:22.024
The Jeju Canola Flower Festival
has begun once again.

07:22.108 --> 07:25.403
Jeju Island is bustling with tourists
who've gathered to see the scenery

07:25.486 --> 07:26.904
embellished with canola flowers.

07:27.530 --> 07:29.157
Today, there are a great variety

07:29.240 --> 07:31.617
of interesting events
planned for couples as well.

07:31.701 --> 07:33.995
So let's interview some of the visitors.

07:34.620 --> 07:37.457
Hello, would you mind
if I asked a few questions?

07:37.540 --> 07:40.168
-No problem.
-So you're here to see the flowers today.

07:40.251 --> 07:41.544
How do you feel about it?

07:42.211 --> 07:43.045
Well…

07:43.671 --> 07:46.132
The flowers remind me of my first love.

07:46.215 --> 07:48.593
Oh, your first love.
Of course, yes, yes.

07:48.676 --> 07:49.969
Go live with her, then.

07:51.053 --> 07:51.888
Oh…

07:51.971 --> 07:53.264
Oh, Hye-ran. No, no.

07:54.474 --> 07:56.893
Mom, is Dad your first love?

07:57.935 --> 07:59.520
Was he your first love?

08:00.354 --> 08:01.856
I don't know.

08:01.939 --> 08:03.274
Yeah, I've forgotten.

08:03.858 --> 08:05.526
Was he your first kiss?

08:05.610 --> 08:08.821
Idiot! Hey, Mom doesn't need that.

08:09.405 --> 08:11.365
You gotta be crazy
to ask a question like that.

08:11.449 --> 08:13.326
-Shut up.
-You little…

08:13.409 --> 08:14.952
-So beautiful.
-Yes.

08:15.036 --> 08:17.663
More beautiful than
the ones in our city.

08:17.747 --> 08:20.458
Did you know canola flowers
smell really intense?

08:22.710 --> 08:25.004
The smell's sweet and really intense.

08:25.880 --> 08:29.592
And the headache you get,
you… you feel like fainting.

08:36.682 --> 08:37.850
I'm hungry.

08:38.726 --> 08:40.978
Why haven't you eaten anything yet?

08:41.687 --> 08:44.398
God, can't you just
get rid of this thing here?

08:44.941 --> 08:46.901
Oh, dinner will be done in a jiffy.

08:53.866 --> 08:56.202
Why would you watch that?
That's so boring.

08:56.702 --> 08:57.620
The expo…

09:00.623 --> 09:01.624
Oh.

09:01.707 --> 09:03.709
MARINATED CHICKEN

09:11.425 --> 09:15.221
Had I known that
spring was truly the spring of my life,

09:16.514 --> 09:20.309
I would've dared
to give myself to love even more.

09:21.602 --> 09:23.354
I still won't marry you.

09:28.067 --> 09:29.902
Oh, today, uh…

09:30.444 --> 09:32.863
Today, the, uh, practice was really tough.

09:32.947 --> 09:34.282
Shut up and walk.

09:59.557 --> 10:06.564
♪ That boy, Sun-bong
Who walks home at eight o'clock ♪

10:07.982 --> 10:14.989
♪ Will I get to see him tomorrow?
I look forward to it ♪

10:16.616 --> 10:19.994
♪ Sun-nam was eating ♪

10:20.536 --> 10:24.081
♪ And now she's gone ♪

10:26.042 --> 10:29.003
♪ Sun-nam was eating ♪

10:30.171 --> 10:33.883
♪ And now she's hiding ♪

10:33.966 --> 10:35.176
I found you!

10:37.428 --> 10:39.597
But spring was ever so fickle.

10:49.607 --> 10:52.193
Just when it felt warm, it would get cold.

10:54.654 --> 10:57.281
Just when it felt cold, it would get hot.

11:00.076 --> 11:02.662
It never ceases to keep you guessing.

11:08.209 --> 11:09.293
We did nothing wrong.

11:11.212 --> 11:12.296
Min-ok.

11:16.133 --> 11:19.470
Morally, I'm a virgin. A virgin.

11:20.096 --> 11:22.932
Legally speaking, I'm single,
so no problem there.

11:23.015 --> 11:24.100
Min-ok.

11:24.767 --> 11:27.770
Why should I need to play caretaker
to your dead wife's kids?

11:28.354 --> 11:30.231
Why do you act like
someone's lording over you?

11:30.314 --> 11:32.066
Why are you saving face constantly?

11:32.149 --> 11:33.859
Next year, you'll be-- You will-- Huh?

11:33.943 --> 11:35.736
Whoa! Whoa!

11:40.533 --> 11:42.952
Are you someone's puppet?

12:03.848 --> 12:07.393
Mom, Jong-gu is your eldest grandson.

12:07.476 --> 12:09.729
No matter where you look
in our family tree,

12:09.812 --> 12:12.106
he'll lead ancestral rites
when you're gone.

12:13.983 --> 12:14.984
What?

12:15.693 --> 12:16.944
Something troubling you?

12:17.737 --> 12:19.071
So what if it is?

12:19.155 --> 12:22.742
You've been taking care of that family.
Now you want something from us?

12:24.034 --> 12:26.203
Grandma, don't you have your own room?

12:26.996 --> 12:28.831
You all eat and sleep in that one room?

12:28.914 --> 12:31.208
Well, if your family's in this state,

12:31.292 --> 12:34.086
the least you can do is
work at a factory or something

12:34.170 --> 12:36.672
and provide for this family.
Why are you helping them?

12:38.966 --> 12:40.634
Do they pay you enough for this work?

12:41.218 --> 12:44.638
I'm not making a living.
This is just so I can buy sweets.

12:44.722 --> 12:45.848
And… and what was that?

12:45.931 --> 12:48.184
Are you a literary girl
yearning for college?

12:48.267 --> 12:50.186
Jong-gu never even went to college.

12:52.188 --> 12:53.022
What?

12:54.231 --> 12:55.900
Do you wanna go to college?

12:57.818 --> 13:01.113
Mom, do you have savings
to give her when we're in this state?

13:01.197 --> 13:02.406
Get paid by your other family.

13:02.490 --> 13:04.450
They should pay you
so you can pay for college.

13:04.533 --> 13:05.951
You're their housekeeper.

13:06.035 --> 13:08.954
If we had spoiled rice,
we wouldn't give it to a dog.

13:09.038 --> 13:10.247
Ow!

13:11.957 --> 13:13.459
Why would you take this down?

13:13.542 --> 13:15.836
It's not yours to take down.
Why did you touch this picture?

13:15.920 --> 13:17.630
-It's not yours!
-What did you expect?

13:17.713 --> 13:20.633
You thought I'd have a picture
of his ex-wife over my head?

13:21.717 --> 13:24.887
Sun-nam, Sun-bong, where were you
when she took down Mom's picture?

13:24.970 --> 13:26.597
How can you eat those right now?

13:26.680 --> 13:28.849
You see this girl
dividing the family?

13:28.933 --> 13:31.560
She's already working them
to be on her side.

13:32.394 --> 13:34.230
You shouldn't have
only bought four ice pops.

13:34.313 --> 13:36.232
-Okay?
-And why would I get five?

13:36.315 --> 13:39.151
-Why suck up to your ex-wife's daughter?
-Min-ok.

13:39.235 --> 13:42.696
Just forget it.
Please tell me you have some sense left.

13:43.280 --> 13:44.156
Min-ok.

13:44.949 --> 13:47.576
That's okay. Just let it go.
Give me my money.

13:47.660 --> 13:50.246
If you do,
I'll leave even if you tell me to stay.

13:50.329 --> 13:51.163
Wait.

13:51.831 --> 13:54.416
No. You borrowed money from a child?

13:54.500 --> 13:55.417
Min-ok.

13:56.335 --> 13:57.211
For what purpose?

13:57.294 --> 14:00.381
-I would never--
-I want the tuition money right now.

14:00.464 --> 14:03.467
You said if I raised your kids,
you'd send me to college.

14:04.593 --> 14:05.678
Oh.

14:06.804 --> 14:08.848
He gave you a home
when you had nowhere to go.

14:08.931 --> 14:10.474
Now you want a sack of cash too?

14:11.183 --> 14:13.269
Give me my money. You promised.

14:14.186 --> 14:15.896
And I even sold your cabbages too.

14:15.980 --> 14:17.106
Why won't you pay me?

14:17.773 --> 14:21.193
You said you'd be too scared of Mom
and that you'd never con me.

14:21.277 --> 14:22.903
Why would he be
afraid of a dead wife?

14:22.987 --> 14:25.030
He should be more scared
of his kids growing fast.

14:25.114 --> 14:26.198
Min-ok.

14:26.282 --> 14:29.869
Next year, by this time,
he'll have three to take care of.

14:29.952 --> 14:31.954
Why would he pay for your tuition?

14:32.663 --> 14:36.792
More importantly, Byeong-cheol
barely has enough cash to provide for us.

14:36.876 --> 14:40.963
Rumor has it he lives with me
because he can't pay me what he owes.

14:41.046 --> 14:43.048
-Na Min-ok.
-What? Damn you, Byeong-cheol!

14:43.132 --> 14:44.717
Sh! Sh.

14:50.764 --> 14:53.267
Get it, my dear? He had you fooled.

14:53.350 --> 14:56.395
See, you're… on your own, Ae-sun.

14:59.189 --> 15:01.859
Of course you're on your own now.
What'd you expect?

15:04.570 --> 15:07.323
In life,
you learn it's every man for himself.

15:07.406 --> 15:09.491
Right now,
best thing is learning to solder.

15:09.575 --> 15:13.454
They teach you the skill, they feed you,
they pay you, and you're a patriot.

15:13.537 --> 15:15.497
There's no better opportunity
for you than this.

15:15.581 --> 15:19.001
And see, it's on the mainland,
just like you always wanted.

15:21.378 --> 15:23.839
If you work like a dog for a few years,

15:23.923 --> 15:26.091
they'll pay you 15,000 won a month.

15:26.175 --> 15:27.885
And if you live at the factory,

15:27.968 --> 15:29.678
you won't have to spend any money.

15:30.763 --> 15:31.639
So you

15:32.181 --> 15:35.351
send us back half the money
each month, all right?

15:35.434 --> 15:37.227
Every single month. Hmm?

15:40.189 --> 15:42.650
The eldest grandson
in the family's debt is yours.

15:42.733 --> 15:45.486
Jong-gu has to do well
for you to find a husband.

15:48.739 --> 15:52.451
You know, Mom said it's easier
to… to just be a cow…

15:54.495 --> 15:56.246
than to be a girl in Jeju.

15:58.374 --> 16:01.085
Jong-gu's been holding
ancestral rites for your father.

16:01.669 --> 16:04.004
Don't talk of things you don't understand.

16:04.088 --> 16:06.173
Oh, Jong-gu's rice is getting cold.

16:06.256 --> 16:07.675
I won't work there.

16:08.759 --> 16:09.593
I won't do it.

16:11.553 --> 16:14.306
I won't take care of
your family or my siblings.

16:15.474 --> 16:16.308
No one.

16:16.392 --> 16:18.352
If you won't work,
where will you go, then?

16:18.936 --> 16:22.064
You wanna live in this tiny house
and add to our worries?

16:22.648 --> 16:24.817
I won't do that. Any of it.

16:25.818 --> 16:27.987
If I keep living like an idiot,
it'll make…

16:29.863 --> 16:31.156
it'll make Mom cry.

16:34.535 --> 16:35.577
Ae-sun,

16:36.578 --> 16:37.579
think it through.

16:38.414 --> 16:39.873
Your mom is gone for good.

16:41.333 --> 16:42.167
Huh?

16:42.876 --> 16:44.294
You won't be

16:45.045 --> 16:47.381
welcome anywhere in the world.

17:12.322 --> 17:13.991
How many rooms are in your house?

17:14.491 --> 17:17.119
Your grandmother's word is law, right?

17:17.870 --> 17:20.372
It is, yeah? It is, right?

17:22.124 --> 17:24.293
What… what happened to you?
Who… who upset you?

17:24.376 --> 17:26.295
"Go to Busan," he said!

17:27.171 --> 17:29.256
He told me to go work at a factory.

17:29.965 --> 17:31.800
I don't have a home anymore.

17:32.551 --> 17:34.845
Sun-nam and Sun-bong took popsicles

17:35.512 --> 17:39.349
from that woman,
and my grandma's family is broke.

17:40.684 --> 17:41.935
And I'm not wanted

17:42.728 --> 17:44.354
anywhere anymore.

17:45.481 --> 17:47.733
The only one who even cares about me,

17:48.442 --> 17:50.611
the only one has to be you, Yang Gwan-sik.

17:51.445 --> 17:52.738
So…

17:55.532 --> 17:57.159
Why me?

17:57.242 --> 18:00.162
Why is it a boy from this island?

18:07.795 --> 18:09.463
There's an outcry with no sound

18:10.547 --> 18:12.925
An eternal handkerchief of nostalgia

18:13.008 --> 18:15.052
That waves
That waves towards the blue sea

18:16.053 --> 18:19.014
I'm going to marry a man
from Seoul, no matter what.

18:19.098 --> 18:22.017
A true heart like a wave, flaps

18:23.018 --> 18:26.146
A true heart flaps like a wave
Just like the wind

18:26.230 --> 18:30.359
I'd never marry a man who doesn't know
what "nostalgia" is. Never!

18:30.984 --> 18:32.611
The first man hanging
In the air

18:33.946 --> 18:35.447
Ah, who is he?

18:36.031 --> 18:38.158
Suspended in the air, the first man

18:38.242 --> 18:40.452
With a blue
And bitter, bitter heart inside

18:41.620 --> 18:44.289
Who cares if you know
what "nostalgia" means?

18:45.082 --> 18:47.793
What about college?
What about being a poet?

18:47.876 --> 18:49.503
And the mainland?

18:52.256 --> 18:53.340
I can't give you everything.

18:56.468 --> 18:57.594
But I'll do one thing,

18:58.178 --> 18:59.680
even if my life depends on it.

18:59.763 --> 19:03.183
Hey, can you at least just say that you'll

19:03.725 --> 19:05.644
give me everything?

19:05.727 --> 19:08.856
Tell me that you'll give me
the stars and the moon.

19:11.358 --> 19:14.236
How can I live with a boy like you?

19:15.362 --> 19:17.614
I don't know. I can't be a liar.

19:18.782 --> 19:23.203
You're actually scared
of your grandmother, too, aren't you?

19:30.252 --> 19:31.712
This is an outcry with no sound

19:31.795 --> 19:32.754
Oh, shut up.

19:38.760 --> 19:40.304
There's an outcry with no sound

19:40.387 --> 19:41.722
Stop it!

19:42.764 --> 19:44.683
An eternal handkerchief of nostalgia

19:45.684 --> 19:47.603
That waves toward the blue sea

20:03.785 --> 20:05.787
You don't have to fight to win.

20:07.497 --> 20:08.540
The way I see it,

20:08.624 --> 20:11.001
even if you're a pro wrestler
like "Headbutting" Kim Il,

20:11.084 --> 20:13.503
it's better to avoid a punch
than to fight back.

20:43.909 --> 20:45.786
Even when we run away,

20:45.869 --> 20:48.080
we have to take what we're owed, don't we?

20:54.253 --> 20:55.128
Sh.

21:23.782 --> 21:27.452
Your grandmother is going
to have me imprisoned for life.

21:44.219 --> 21:45.429
You sure you won't regret this?

21:46.179 --> 21:47.723
Because once we leave Jeju,

21:48.515 --> 21:50.517
there won't be any turning back anymore.

21:51.518 --> 21:53.312
Uh, damn it.

21:53.395 --> 21:55.522
You don't get
a second opportunity in life.

21:57.149 --> 22:00.402
If your life and my life
join together as one,

22:00.485 --> 22:02.654
we tough it out together,
whether we live or die.

22:06.283 --> 22:08.076
So if you're afraid, then go now.

22:09.995 --> 22:11.371
Just run home, okay?

22:15.584 --> 22:18.920
In the…19 years I've lived, I, uh…

22:23.508 --> 22:24.968
I've never felt this excited.

22:34.019 --> 22:36.521
-How fast is your 100 meters?
-Twenty-four seconds.

22:37.606 --> 22:38.815
All right. Let's go.

22:45.072 --> 22:47.699
Who can stop spring
when it arrives inevitably?

22:47.783 --> 22:50.619
FEMALE RUNAWAY PREVENTION PERIOD

22:50.702 --> 22:52.621
Springtime in Jeju

22:52.704 --> 22:54.706
arrived particularly early

22:55.540 --> 22:56.458
that year.

23:05.217 --> 23:07.302
To celebrate
a springtime revolution,

23:07.386 --> 23:09.262
the May 16 military coup,

23:09.346 --> 23:12.432
all provinces of the nation
are preparing for festivals.

23:12.516 --> 23:13.350
For this…

23:13.934 --> 23:15.310
That spring,

23:15.811 --> 23:19.314
their coup, as ambitious
as their first voyage…

23:19.856 --> 23:21.775
The president
started a revolution

23:21.858 --> 23:25.028
when the nation needed protection from
Kim Shin-jo's team of North Korea.

23:25.612 --> 23:28.073
…wasn't as revolutionary as they'd hoped.

23:28.740 --> 23:30.325
Provincial ID, please.

23:33.453 --> 23:35.080
Provincial ID.

23:36.331 --> 23:39.167
Without ID,
we'll consider you DPRK agents.

23:41.628 --> 23:44.172
You said you're both adults.
Let's see your IDs.

23:45.674 --> 23:48.009
Why do you look scared,
sitting in a corner like this?

23:48.510 --> 23:51.304
What are you saying? I don't understand.

23:53.265 --> 23:55.725
-Uh, sir.
-I think you're minors.

23:56.726 --> 23:59.688
Sir? We're not, um…

24:00.564 --> 24:01.982
You're both runaways, huh?

24:03.859 --> 24:06.319
How'd you end up together? Wow.

24:06.903 --> 24:10.115
Oh, what are you trying to say, sir?
I don't understand at all.

24:11.199 --> 24:13.994
Kids are so ballsy these days. Shit.

24:14.077 --> 24:16.246
How dare you
get on this ship by yourselves?

24:18.748 --> 24:19.666
So throw us over.

24:19.749 --> 24:20.584
What?

24:23.128 --> 24:24.421
Throw us overboard here.

24:25.839 --> 24:28.049
What makes you so brash?

24:28.133 --> 24:30.927
Is your family rich?
Is your father a politician or what?

24:33.847 --> 24:35.056
Throw us over.

24:36.641 --> 24:37.476
What's that?

24:38.185 --> 24:40.395
Come on, girl. What?

24:40.479 --> 24:42.147
What are you?

24:42.230 --> 24:43.356
Married.

24:46.067 --> 24:47.027
What?

24:47.944 --> 24:49.905
Husband and wife.

24:51.281 --> 24:54.284
We're married because we're adults.
How can kids get married?

24:54.868 --> 24:55.785
Let's go, babe.

25:22.479 --> 25:23.563
So what are you two?

25:24.189 --> 25:25.190
Husband and wife.

25:30.737 --> 25:32.072
What do I do with those?

25:32.155 --> 25:34.115
Why are you being so rude to us, ma'am?

25:34.783 --> 25:35.909
Are these really yours?

25:35.992 --> 25:37.994
Are people in Busan
typically this rude to customers?

25:38.078 --> 25:39.287
We're all adults here.

25:39.371 --> 25:41.998
-Did you steal these?
-They're his grandmother's rings.

25:51.007 --> 25:52.259
I need to see your IDs.

25:52.342 --> 25:53.176
We forgot them.

25:53.260 --> 25:56.680
Oh, yes, I'm sure.
You just forgot, yeah.

25:56.763 --> 26:00.767
-I was born in, uh, '49.
-That was the Year of the Tiger.

26:00.850 --> 26:02.894
-'49, Year of the Tiger.
-Year of the Ox, dear.

26:04.771 --> 26:06.773
What are these? You stole 'em or what?

26:08.191 --> 26:10.110
-Are you a thief, kid?
-We're runaways.

26:20.662 --> 26:22.914
NAMPOJANG INN

26:22.998 --> 26:25.166
We don't have a provincial ID

26:25.792 --> 26:27.419
or a national ID.

26:28.295 --> 26:31.089
We were robbed,

26:31.881 --> 26:34.009
so we don't have anything with us, unless…

26:35.927 --> 26:36.803
Take it out.

26:46.646 --> 26:48.690
Can you let us have a room for this?

26:50.692 --> 26:51.610
Guess not.

26:52.527 --> 26:55.405
Uh, you could see if a pawn shop wants it.

26:55.488 --> 26:56.489
Newlyweds?

26:57.824 --> 26:59.326
You look like newlyweds.

26:59.409 --> 27:01.161
Are you kids on your honeymoon?

27:03.121 --> 27:04.956
Huh. Hmm.

27:05.040 --> 27:06.207
No problem.

27:06.291 --> 27:07.667
You pay us tomorrow, okay?

27:07.751 --> 27:12.005
Wow, how kind of you.
Are we running a charity, dear?

27:12.088 --> 27:14.341
Their wallets were stolen
on their honeymoon.

27:14.424 --> 27:16.009
They must be so upset.

27:19.387 --> 27:21.556
Wait, are you giving us a room?

27:23.099 --> 27:25.018
Don't feel bad about being robbed here.

27:25.644 --> 27:28.188
Busan's hospitality is top-notch.

27:48.792 --> 27:50.752
You could voice your opinion, you know.

27:51.503 --> 27:53.129
You that scared of your grandma?

27:54.339 --> 27:55.548
I'm not afraid of her.

27:56.925 --> 28:00.845
Did she say you're naughty if you speak up
and then virtuous if you run away?

28:02.430 --> 28:04.099
I'm not afraid of my grandmother.

28:06.101 --> 28:07.143
Fine, you're not.

28:10.438 --> 28:12.607
I was afraid of her
giving you a hard time.

28:23.451 --> 28:27.122
Are you… okay with giving up on athletics?

28:28.498 --> 28:29.749
I'm not even that good.

28:31.584 --> 28:33.586
I only went 'cause you get milk and bread.

28:35.046 --> 28:36.339
What are you, a hog?

28:42.846 --> 28:45.265
You should… take the GED.

28:46.683 --> 28:47.976
I'll work at the factory.

28:58.445 --> 29:01.030
Do you know the reason
I'm going to marry Yang Gwan-sik,

29:01.114 --> 29:03.199
the least cool boy in all of Jeju?

29:07.412 --> 29:08.496
You are

29:10.081 --> 29:11.040
like steel.

29:14.127 --> 29:17.338
We may get hungry,
but you'll never break my heart.

29:21.259 --> 29:23.928
Even if I was given
a gold or a silver axe,

29:24.012 --> 29:25.722
I would choose the steel axe.

29:26.306 --> 29:27.849
The steel one's useful.

29:29.350 --> 29:31.895
Nobody would give you
a gold or silver axe anyway.

29:32.479 --> 29:35.899
Yeah, the least cool boy I know.

29:47.202 --> 29:48.495
You said we're married.

29:51.831 --> 29:53.124
Seems like we're not.

29:57.587 --> 29:59.547
Uh, It doesn't seem like it at all now.

30:07.430 --> 30:08.515
Yang Gwan-sik.

30:13.436 --> 30:15.188
Excuse me.

30:25.949 --> 30:27.116
Jeez.

30:27.867 --> 30:30.453
Why are you giddy
when she ripped off your rings?

30:30.537 --> 30:33.248
She, uh, did swipe
your yellow dress, right?

30:34.582 --> 30:36.876
You know, the boy's family,

30:37.377 --> 30:41.130
Gwan-sik, right?
At his house, their gold frog is gone.

30:41.673 --> 30:44.384
She poached their gold frog
and their son too.

30:47.136 --> 30:49.556
You're so giddy. Is this fun for you?

30:50.890 --> 30:53.852
The kid's grandma,
see, she almost fainted.

30:53.935 --> 30:55.979
Man, oh man, they're rash.

30:56.062 --> 30:58.481
How'd they imagine
running off to Busan like that?

30:58.565 --> 31:01.776
But rumor has it, they may have
caused a riot on that boat.

31:04.112 --> 31:07.282
They've been saying
that Ae-sun was behind the whole thing.

31:07.365 --> 31:09.075
Jeez.

31:11.077 --> 31:13.746
Ae-sun is a romantic, huh?

31:13.830 --> 31:17.584
-Well, come on, they're lovers on the run.
-What's the point of it all?

31:17.667 --> 31:18.668
Who cares about romance?

31:18.751 --> 31:21.462
Once food becomes a problem,
then they'll start to hate each other.

31:22.046 --> 31:23.798
What's being hungry at that age, huh?

31:23.882 --> 31:27.510
Right now, even if all day,
they just eat tangerines together

31:27.594 --> 31:30.346
on a cold marble floor,
they'd still be happy.

31:31.806 --> 31:32.640
Min-ok.

31:34.934 --> 31:35.768
Were you happy?

31:36.561 --> 31:39.188
I've never eaten tangerines with you,
my dear.

31:41.524 --> 31:42.400
Now we could.

31:44.068 --> 31:45.153
Anyone home?

31:49.365 --> 31:51.242
Write down the outfit
you think she wore, okay?

31:51.993 --> 31:55.079
-Evidently, she stole your clothes.
-Are you going after them?

31:55.580 --> 31:57.874
You're like a bounty hunter.
That's so cool.

31:58.583 --> 32:01.794
How will you find them?
You never will. You never will.

32:02.962 --> 32:05.131
Stop talking and write it down now.

32:05.715 --> 32:08.009
-I don't know what she wore.
-What?

32:08.092 --> 32:11.429
I sell fashion door-to-door.
I have so many clothes.

32:12.055 --> 32:13.765
Damn it.

32:13.848 --> 32:15.058
Oh man.

32:15.141 --> 32:17.101
It's their first night, probably.

32:17.936 --> 32:20.188
-Ah.
-Shut up.

32:22.440 --> 32:24.651
Busan's hospitality is top-notch.

32:25.985 --> 32:28.655
This is Busan's crown jewel.

32:28.738 --> 32:29.864
It'd be a shame

32:30.531 --> 32:32.367
for you to miss tasting a bit.

32:34.827 --> 32:37.288
Is this all free of charge?

32:38.331 --> 32:40.458
Busan is a huge city.

32:42.085 --> 32:43.544
The floor's all warm now.

32:44.128 --> 32:47.715
So just finish drinking the soju
and get some sleep, all right?

32:48.299 --> 32:50.385
If both of you lie down
on this nice warm floor,

32:50.468 --> 32:54.597
then you will melt like
a little butter in a frying pan.

32:55.139 --> 32:57.934
But before you melt on the floor…

33:00.311 --> 33:01.604
…take your time

33:01.688 --> 33:03.314
and enjoy

33:03.940 --> 33:04.774
your night.

33:06.943 --> 33:09.529
Oh, well, it is your honeymoon, after all.

33:11.698 --> 33:15.368
Oh dear, you're both flushed.
Please just get right to it.

33:15.451 --> 33:17.704
You're in the best place
for a night like this.

33:17.787 --> 33:21.290
Here, even the most unschooled men
learn everything there is to know.

33:21.374 --> 33:22.542
Stop it, miss.

33:23.668 --> 33:24.794
Oh dear.

33:24.877 --> 33:25.753
Please just stop.

33:32.719 --> 33:33.553
Give it everything.

33:50.153 --> 33:51.529
Give it everything.

33:53.698 --> 33:55.241
Give it everything.

34:09.672 --> 34:13.009
Jaecheop-guk for sale. Jaecheop-guk.

34:14.969 --> 34:18.264
Jaecheop-guk for sale. Jaecheop-guk.

34:31.569 --> 34:32.904
Is the toilet clean?

34:33.905 --> 34:34.739
Huh?

34:35.406 --> 34:36.240
Yeah.

34:37.283 --> 34:38.534
It's completely fine.

34:40.953 --> 34:41.788
Huh?

34:42.371 --> 34:43.581
Did you break the fan?

34:46.918 --> 34:47.752
Huh?

34:53.091 --> 34:54.759
Um, maybe a screw fell out.

34:56.177 --> 34:58.971
Well, just leave it, then.

34:59.555 --> 35:02.183
-Okay?
-Okay. But what if they charge us for it?

35:02.683 --> 35:05.812
But see, Busan's hospitality is top-notch.

35:21.410 --> 35:22.328
BILL
TOTAL: 640 WON

35:23.788 --> 35:26.040
Didn't she say all that stuff
she gave us was on the house?

35:26.124 --> 35:28.376
Hmm.

35:29.127 --> 35:31.629
Ow. What's this?

35:32.130 --> 35:32.964
What's this?

35:34.382 --> 35:35.633
Ow, that hurt.

35:46.894 --> 35:48.146
What's going on?

35:52.150 --> 35:53.609
What? What is it?

35:55.695 --> 35:58.406
What? What's going on, hmm?

35:58.489 --> 36:00.199
-Our suitcase.
-Hmm?

36:00.283 --> 36:02.118
-Where's our suitcase?
-Suitcase?

36:04.370 --> 36:05.997
Were any other rooms robbed?

36:06.080 --> 36:07.832
Were there guests
who seemed strange?

36:07.915 --> 36:10.251
-What are you suggesting, miss?
-What?

36:11.794 --> 36:13.546
Stop playing around and pay up.

36:13.629 --> 36:16.799
The charges are for room service
and for breaking the fan mount.

36:16.883 --> 36:20.219
The broken mount is the evidence.
Why would it be broken though?

36:20.303 --> 36:22.555
-The thief was tip-toeing in the dark.
-Stop!

36:23.848 --> 36:26.434
You guys broke the fan.
I know it was you two.

36:26.517 --> 36:28.311
-Why would we do it?
-Well, hold on.

36:28.394 --> 36:30.229
Look, it's possible
your guests saw something.

36:30.313 --> 36:31.397
-Maybe we could ask.
-Mm-hmm.

36:31.480 --> 36:33.691
Let's call ourselves
the hotel where they rob guests.

36:33.774 --> 36:35.359
Ah, maybe your wife saw something.

36:35.443 --> 36:36.944
-Yeah.
-Sorry?

36:37.570 --> 36:39.780
I never saw you with any bag at all.

36:40.489 --> 36:43.701
-I remember you came here empty-handed.
-And you will sit right here.

36:44.243 --> 36:45.620
-Hey.
-Yeah?

36:45.703 --> 36:48.289
Did you see these people
bring a suitcase with them?

36:48.873 --> 36:49.916
Mm-mm.

36:49.999 --> 36:51.584
Ah, what?

36:52.293 --> 36:54.962
Oh, this came from the suitcase we had.

36:55.546 --> 36:57.632
-But it was left on the floor.
-Wow!

36:57.715 --> 37:00.384
You didn't even have a suitcase,
so we took pity on you kids.

37:00.468 --> 37:01.969
Now you want us to give you one?

37:02.053 --> 37:05.181
No. No, we set our suitcase
by this window.

37:05.264 --> 37:07.850
-You gave me the key.
-You must be so upset.

37:08.851 --> 37:09.727
Right, well,

37:10.603 --> 37:11.729
why don't we call the police?

37:12.605 --> 37:13.814
Should we call them

37:14.357 --> 37:16.734
and tell them
that these kids here are runaways?

37:17.318 --> 37:20.071
Busan's hospitality
is top-notch, huh?

37:20.613 --> 37:22.865
This is Busan's crown jewel.

37:22.949 --> 37:25.743
It'd be such a shame
if you didn't get to taste this.

37:32.667 --> 37:33.501
MISSING PERSONS

37:33.584 --> 37:35.294
YANG GWAN-SIK, MALE, AGE 19
HANDSOME

37:35.378 --> 37:37.088
OH AE-SUN, FEMALE, AGE 18
VIXEN-LIKE

37:38.130 --> 37:39.006
Yes.

37:43.636 --> 37:44.512
Look, ma'am,

37:44.595 --> 37:47.056
you may as well search
for them at Jagalchi Market.

37:47.139 --> 37:50.643
How in the world will you find kids
who were so determined to run away?

37:51.894 --> 37:56.607
I'm running out of time, Mother.
Enough about your dreams already.

37:56.691 --> 37:58.609
I've gotta go, okay?

37:59.610 --> 38:00.528
Dream reading?

38:04.365 --> 38:07.285
And why'd the rooster snatch the kids?

38:08.077 --> 38:11.247
Are you telling me
you'd like some chicken for supper?

38:11.330 --> 38:13.040
Cock-a-doodle-doo.

38:13.124 --> 38:14.417
Newlyweds, huh?

38:14.500 --> 38:17.003
Here's the fried chicken
you ordered.

38:17.086 --> 38:18.462
Enjoy your meal!

38:18.546 --> 38:20.631
Do you take me for a moron? Huh?

38:20.715 --> 38:22.591
You really thought you had me fooled?

38:22.675 --> 38:24.844
Why did you give us a room and alcohol?

38:24.927 --> 38:27.847
-Without bags or any money at all?
-Stop yapping.

38:28.556 --> 38:30.266
Let's call the police now.

38:30.349 --> 38:34.020
Let's call the cops and have your mother
come by boat from Jeju.

38:34.103 --> 38:35.813
I should break this girl's legs, damn it.

38:35.896 --> 38:37.606
How did you know
we're from Jeju?

38:43.195 --> 38:44.363
Get out. Yeah, go.

38:44.447 --> 38:46.907
-I'll just pretend it's bad luck. Go!
-Wait a minute.

38:47.408 --> 38:49.618
How did you know we're from Jeju? How?

38:50.911 --> 38:53.706
Shall I call the police?
How about we argue over every detail?

38:53.789 --> 38:54.665
Boarding passes.

38:55.458 --> 38:57.585
I know you robbed us.
They were in our bag.

38:59.253 --> 39:00.087
You idiot.

39:00.838 --> 39:01.964
You idiot.

39:03.549 --> 39:04.717
Oh, my bag.

39:05.593 --> 39:06.427
Oh.

39:07.011 --> 39:08.471
Our suitcase, wow.

39:08.554 --> 39:09.722
Give it back.

39:10.598 --> 39:12.558
Oh, that suitcase is all we have left.

39:13.851 --> 39:16.771
Oh, my mom's picture is in that suitcase.

39:16.854 --> 39:19.190
Oh, my suitcase.

39:20.775 --> 39:23.694
You kept making the room hotter.
Then you kept giving us drinks.

39:24.278 --> 39:27.448
You made sure we were fast asleep
to be able to steal our suitcase.

39:27.531 --> 39:29.950
Wait, all the towels
they have were stolen too.

39:30.034 --> 39:32.495
SUBONGYONG SAUNA
NAMPO BARBERSHOP - JUNGANG SAUNA

39:33.245 --> 39:34.455
You thieves.

39:35.081 --> 39:36.415
You… you thieves.

39:37.666 --> 39:39.001
You have evidence?

39:39.835 --> 39:42.463
-The boarding passes! You saw them.
-So what if we did?

39:42.546 --> 39:44.715
-Where's the evidence?
-Where's the evidence?

39:45.966 --> 39:47.635
Leave while
we're still being nice.

39:48.511 --> 39:51.722
You know, before we sell the both of you.

39:53.015 --> 39:54.683
Leave while
we're still being nice.

39:57.937 --> 40:00.314
The suitcase was all we had.

40:03.567 --> 40:05.903
That was the only picture of Mom I had.

40:08.114 --> 40:10.324
The gold frog was in there too.

40:12.410 --> 40:14.662
That's what we get for begging.

40:16.080 --> 40:18.249
The same as
those little storybook children

40:18.332 --> 40:22.128
who were beguiled by breadcrumbs
and captured by a witch.

40:24.046 --> 40:24.964
I don't know them.

40:26.715 --> 40:28.175
Hansel and Gretel.

40:29.844 --> 40:31.011
Never heard of it.

40:34.056 --> 40:38.185
Oh, well, I always thought those kids
were the biggest morons.

40:38.853 --> 40:40.813
They shoved candy in their mouths

40:41.730 --> 40:44.525
with no clue about
how close they were to being eaten.

40:50.072 --> 40:51.490
What happened to those kids?

40:52.450 --> 40:53.284
Did they live?

40:54.326 --> 40:55.619
They killed her.

40:56.996 --> 40:59.165
-She killed the kids?
-No.

41:00.040 --> 41:01.834
They killed her.

41:05.296 --> 41:07.089
The children pushed the witch…

41:09.091 --> 41:10.551
…into an oven, and…

41:11.635 --> 41:13.637
and they burned her alive.

41:14.722 --> 41:15.556
Ae-sun.

41:16.056 --> 41:17.516
They killed her,

41:18.350 --> 41:21.437
took all her silver,
gold, and all her treasures,

41:22.688 --> 41:25.316
and they lived happily ever after.

41:27.067 --> 41:27.985
Uh, Ae-sun…

41:28.486 --> 41:30.529
They really were something.

41:47.254 --> 41:49.798
It's all on the house. All free.

41:49.882 --> 41:51.717
Busan's hospitality is top-notch.

41:51.800 --> 41:54.386
Drink all of that in this warm room,

41:54.470 --> 41:58.140
and you'll melt on the floor
like butter in a frying pan.

41:59.183 --> 42:02.937
-This and this and this right here.
-Oh, what happened to your fan?

42:03.979 --> 42:05.898
Damn it! It happened yesterday.

42:05.981 --> 42:09.276
Lunatics got in,
making a total mess of the place.

42:10.986 --> 42:12.613
Hurry. Let me climb on your back.

42:12.696 --> 42:14.281
-Oh, okay.
-Hurry.

42:14.365 --> 42:17.993
Ah, these kids came in here
and made us so mad.

42:18.077 --> 42:20.538
I wanted to strangle them,
but I let them go.

42:21.205 --> 42:22.957
We're all polite here, you know?

42:47.398 --> 42:48.524
What is it?

42:50.901 --> 42:52.027
Excuse us.

42:53.696 --> 42:55.406
I think I've had enough freebies.

42:55.489 --> 42:58.242
-Those "free things"?
-If you get drunk, they'll rob you.

42:58.325 --> 43:00.786
She said to drink it all
and melt like butter, right?

43:01.579 --> 43:02.454
Who are you guys?

43:02.538 --> 43:05.457
Listen. Just don't
turn off the lights, okay?

43:22.516 --> 43:24.101
Why isn't she sleeping?

43:26.937 --> 43:28.188
Hey, bug.

43:33.027 --> 43:34.903
Well, we're not making money tonight.

43:36.864 --> 43:38.616
Charge her double for soju tomorrow.

43:39.116 --> 43:39.950
Oh man.

43:42.328 --> 43:43.329
Oh man.

43:54.423 --> 43:57.009
The gold frog
and Mom's picture is priority. Got it?

43:58.802 --> 44:00.554
We look for our stuff first,

44:00.638 --> 44:03.182
and if we can't find it,
we take their cash box, okay?

44:07.561 --> 44:10.522
We'd be at a loss still.
Frog's worth more than their box.

44:11.106 --> 44:12.524
You see, we're not stealing.

44:18.822 --> 44:21.408
We need our things
to live together, right?

44:24.078 --> 44:25.079
Gwan-sik.

44:26.163 --> 44:28.332
You must be the head of the house, 'kay?

44:35.756 --> 44:37.675
Baby.

44:43.013 --> 44:43.972
Baby.

44:50.396 --> 44:51.230
Let's go.

45:20.259 --> 45:21.593
It's not there.

45:22.136 --> 45:23.053
Not there.

45:38.068 --> 45:39.653
Hey. Hey.

45:39.737 --> 45:40.612
Don't open it.

45:40.696 --> 45:41.905
Don't open it.

45:41.989 --> 45:43.657
Cash. Cash. Cash.

45:44.324 --> 45:45.325
Cashbox.

46:21.236 --> 46:22.237
Got it.

46:43.967 --> 46:47.513
Let's just go.
Go. I'll get you a new one.

46:58.941 --> 47:00.150
Run! Come on!

47:03.487 --> 47:04.822
Hey! Stop!

47:05.697 --> 47:07.866
-Stop!
-Hey!

47:08.951 --> 47:09.952
The cashbox.

47:10.452 --> 47:12.246
-Lady!
-Put it down.

47:12.830 --> 47:15.290
-Right. 24 seconds. 24 seconds.
-Put down the cashbox.

47:15.374 --> 47:17.376
-Damn it, you asshole.
-Put down the cashbox.

47:17.459 --> 47:19.086
I swear I'll beat this girl to a pulp.

47:21.171 --> 47:22.589
I'm done for.

47:22.673 --> 47:23.674
Oh, just go.

47:23.757 --> 47:25.843
Go! Just go!

47:25.926 --> 47:28.929
You want us to sell this girl? Huh?
Somewhere she won't be found?

47:31.515 --> 47:32.850
That's the pit of my stomach.

47:34.601 --> 47:36.478
My stomach, my stomach.

47:36.562 --> 47:38.063
Put it down before I lose it.

47:38.564 --> 47:41.024
-Come at me. Let's do it.
-Put it down, damn it!

47:46.697 --> 47:49.032
-Okay, let up a bit. I'm dying.
-Quiet, you.

47:49.116 --> 47:51.368
Damn it. Put it down. Now!

47:51.451 --> 47:53.328
-Lady, lady.
-Look at that punk.

47:54.079 --> 47:55.622
Yeah. Just go.

47:56.206 --> 47:58.417
-Put it down.
-Yeah, run along, asshole.

47:58.500 --> 48:00.961
Go, go, asshole. Go.

48:02.880 --> 48:04.089
That damn punk.

48:05.674 --> 48:07.509
I said, put it down, you scum!

48:08.886 --> 48:10.762
That's right. There you go.

48:11.471 --> 48:13.974
What the…
what the hell is he doing? What?

48:22.566 --> 48:26.403
Mom's first love
was the karate master Choi Bae-dal.

48:28.780 --> 48:29.823
And Mom

48:29.907 --> 48:31.533
was "Headbutting" Kim Il.

51:24.372 --> 51:29.002
"THE SAME SKY, THE SAME STARS,
ETCHED IN THE SAME HEARTS"
